{"text": "People show a tendency to trust ideas that correspond to their beliefs, even though there is little or no objective evidence to support them. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Such ideas may eventually turn out to be false, if the assumptions underlying them largely rely on subjective observations. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Careful thinkers thus try to test their existing beliefs, rather than simply maintaining them. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> When new evidence does not support the idea that they have entertained, they reexamine it from alternative viewpoints. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This inspires them to go about challenging the problematic belief. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Therefore, thinking reflectively about the existing beliefs helps people adjust them according to available evidence. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Furthermore, it enables people to become less likely to accept new ideas just because they are tempting or consistent with what they have long believed. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Although individuals differ considerably in their belief systems, those who objectify and test their own beliefs tend to think more critically than those who do not.", "alignment": {"characters": ["P", "e", "o", "p", "l", "e", " ", "s", "h", "o", "w", " ", "a", " ", "t", "e", "n", "d", "e", "n", "c", "y", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "r", "u", "s", "t", " ", "i", "d", "e", "a", "s", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "c", "o", "r", "r", "e", "s", "p", "o", "n", "d", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", "i", "r", " ", "b", "e", "l", "i", "e", "f", "s", ",", " ", "e", "v", "e", "n", " ", "t", "h", "o", "u", "g", "h", " ", "t", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "i", "s", " ", "l", "i", "t", "t", "l", "e", " ", "o", "r", " ", "n", "o", " ", "o", "b", "j", "e", "c", "t", "i", "v", "e", " ", "e", "v", "i", "d", "e", "n", "c", "e", " ", "t", "o", " ", "s", "u", "p", "p", "o", "r", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", "m", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", 